# Documentation: 12-push.http REST client collection.
# - Exercises browser push subscription registration and unsubscription endpoints.
# - Use a real browser-generated subscription payload if you want to validate end-to-end delivery instead of schema acceptance only.
# - These requests are written for the VS Code REST Client extension and use its response-variable syntax extensively.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8787
@json = application/json
@seedPassword = Test@1234
@memberEmail = member.1.seed-gym-1@seed.gym.test
@endpoint = https://push.seed.gym.test/subscriptions/rest-client-endpoint

# @name memberLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "member.1.seed-gym-1@seed.gym.test",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

### Subscribe the current user to push notifications
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint": "{{endpoint}}",
  "keys": {
    "p256dh": "test-p256dh-key",
    "auth": "test-auth-key"
  }
}

### Unsubscribe the endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/unsubscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{memberLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint": "{{endpoint}}"
}
